            "target_entity_instance": "base FGYM",
            "target_entity_type": "Source",
            "paragraph": "As mentioned earlier, the objective of this study is to integrate the dummy variables for the stand development stage and continuous climatic variables into the base FGYM framework.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "site class index model (SCI)",
            "source_entity_type": "SourceComponent",
            "relation": "USES_PHYSICAL_SCHEME",
            "target_entity_instance": "Richards function",
            "target_entity_type": "PhysicalScheme",
            "paragraph": "To evaluate site conditions, the relationship between stand mean height (TH) and stand age (t) was fitted using a series of commonly used theoretical models (e.g., Mistchlinch, Weibull, Korf, Richard) or empirical models (e.g., Hossfeld; West, 2009). Model performance was assessed based on the adjusted coefficient of determination (adjR\u00b2), mean absolute error percentage (MAE%), and root mean square error percentage (RMSE%). The results demonstrated that the Richards function significantly outperformed the other models, showing significantly superior goodness of fit.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": false,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "stand basal area model (BAS)",
